## Role-and-skill dispatcher (Hornero)

Hornero ships roles and skills under `<path-to-hornero>/roles/` and
`<path-to-hornero>/skills/`, indexed by `<path-to-hornero>/CATALOG.md`.

When a prompt arrives:

1. **Slash commands win** if the user typed one. Hornero ships these:
   `/orchestrate` (PM as cross-functional orchestrator), `/review` (direct
   multi-role-review), `/role <name> <task>` (single named role), `/kickoff`,
   `/catalog`, `/extract-lesson`. Definitions in
   `<path-to-hornero>/.claude/commands/` (or `~/.claude/commands/` if installed).
2. Scan `<path-to-hornero>/CATALOG.md` — a one-line-per-entry index of every
   shipped role and skill.
3. Match the prompt against role triggers and skill `description:`/`scenarios:`
   frontmatter fields. Explicit naming by the user always wins.
4. **Declare the choice in one line** before doing the work, e.g.
   `Adopting `tester` / `regression-test` — prompt names a shipped bug.`
   The user can redirect with a single word.
5. Load the chosen `roles/<role>/ROLE.md` and `skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`.
   Don't load every skill up front.
6. If two or more roles match strongly, escalate — to `/orchestrate` when the
   integrating thread is a customer job, else to `/review`. If nothing
   matches, say so — don't fabricate a skill.

The dispatcher does NOT fire for trivial edits (typos, renames, formatting)
or when the user explicitly disables it ("just answer directly").

Full protocol in `<path-to-hornero>/DISPATCHER.md` — host-agnostic, loaded
on demand by both Claude Code (`<path-to-hornero>/CLAUDE.md`) and Codex
(`<path-to-hornero>/AGENTS.md`).

